# The plan launch_screens.sh runs (one name from plans/, first non-comment line). Change it by commit.
# stage1_select starts with "wait_mark SCREENS PRECONDITIONS OK": it trains nothing until a person records
# SCREENS ORDER 0 as met (touch ~/planck/runs/SCREENS/marks/SCREENS_PRECONDITIONS_OK on the PC, after the
# preconditions and the cap check are logged in SCREENS.txt). stage2_select waits the same way for
# SCREENS_STAGE_2_SMOKES_RECORDED (each flag's eager smoke run on the PC, labelled smoke, logged in its notes.txt:
# mem_fit, tok/s for the GPU HOURS factors, leak self-test; AMENDMENT C1-b: every run eager, no compile gate).
# stage2_s006x (S006's C3 extension, SCREENS.txt STAGE 2 SELECTION RESULT) waits for SCREENS_STAGE_2_SELECTION_DONE
# and stops at SCREENS_S006_EXTENSION_DONE (the seed sets need its pick).
# stage2_seeds (ORDER 2's seed sets, S006 cut by ORDER's cap rule: SCREENS.txt S006 EXTENSION RESULT / STAGE 2
# SEEDS LAUNCH CHECK) waits for SCREENS_S006_EXTENSION_DONE and stops at SCREENS_STAGE_2_SEEDS_DONE (the stage 2
# verdicts need a person). Its BASE lines are skipped by the queue (scored in stage 1).
# stage2_s006_seeds (S006's seed sets at g 2 with C6's IND runs at g 1, after AMENDMENT S006-REINSTATE in SCREENS.txt)
# waits for SCREENS_STAGE_2_SEEDS_DONE and stops at SCREENS_STAGE_2_S006_SEEDS_DONE. It runs from its own bundle,
# planck-kit/planck_s006.bundle, started by experiments/screens/s006_waiter.sh after stage2_seeds ends cleanly.
# Seed plans come from screens.py seeds.
stage2_s006_seeds
